nodes.body:
@ivanusto thanks for the weight-free replay — that narrows it correctly.

Agreed: the indexer is only built for `compress_ratio==4` (64 states), so stock `fp8_ds_mla` never puts a 2-state page in front of `get_paged_mqa_logits_metadata`. Our `nvfp4_ds_mla` / B12X / FlashInfer sparse path *does* route compress-128 into that call site, which is why the gate is required there and a no-op elsewhere.

A uniform compress-128 guarded vs unguarded test would be welcome if you run one; otherwise the recipe + overlay in https://github.com/maci0/vllm-spark-0731 already pins it on 2x GB10.

@ivanusto merged [maci0/vllm#1](https://github.com/maci0/vllm/pull/1) onto this branch (`570821ee9`). The call-site file is now in the PR: `tests/v1/attention/test_indexer_paged_mqa_gate.py`, next to the existing `test_indexer_paged_mqa_metadata.py` helper coverage.

Kept both of your call-site choices: `DeepSeek-V2-Lite-Chat` for the throwaway config, and `raising=False` on the `is_deep_gemm_supported` monkeypatch so an unpatched tree fails on the routing decision rather than a missing symbol.

Skip-path `torch.empty` stays as-is. `zero_()` remains a follow-up if review asks.

